{
  "category": "Jet Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It has superb accuracy. The water it shoots out can strike even moving prey from more than 300 feet.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its dorsal fin as a suction pad, it clings to a MANTINE's underside to scavenge for leftovers.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "To escape from an attacker, it may shoot water out of its mouth, then use that force to swim backward.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "REMORAID sucks in water, then expels it at high velocity using its abdominal muscles to shoot down flying prey. When evolution draws near, this POKéMON travels downstream from rivers.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "REMORAID sucks in water, then expels it at high velocity using its abdominal muscles to shoot down flying prey. When evolution draws near, this POKéMON travels downstream from rivers.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A REMORAID uses its abdominal muscles to forcefully expel swallowed water, then shoot down flying prey. When evolution approaches, it travels down rivers.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its dorsal fin as a suction pad, it clings to a MANTINE’s underside to scavenge for leftovers.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has superb accuracy. The water it shoots out can strike even moving prey from more than 100 yards.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It squirts water forcefully from its mouth to shoot down flying prey.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It clings to MANTINE to feed on the big Pokémon’s scraps. This is an adaptation to avoid foes.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It forcefully squirts water. The water jet never misses prey even if the REMORAID is deep in the sea.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has superb accuracy. The water it shoots out can strike moving prey from more than 300 feet away.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its dorsal fin as a suction pad, it clings to a MANTINE’s underside to scavenge for leftovers.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It forcefully squirts water. The water jet never misses prey even if the Remoraid is deep in the sea.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "It forcefully squirts water. The water jet never misses prey even if the Remoraid is deep in the sea.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "The water they shoot from their mouths can hit moving prey from more than 300 feet away.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
